Upstream attribution
--------------------

This repository is a fork of lizthegrey/bsky-mcp-server
(https://github.com/lizthegrey/bsky-mcp-server). The original project and the
work contributed to it are credited here: the upstream code, its authors, and
its contributors are the source of the baseline this fork builds on, and their
original MIT licence terms are acknowledged.

What this fork changes
----------------------

Notable areas where this fork differs from upstream (the README's "Differences
from upstream" section is the long version):

- AI-preference enforcement via `community.lexicon.preference.ai` records,
  applied by every content-fetching tool, with tombstones preserving order.
- Mention handling (`get-mention-context`, `run-mention-monitor`,
  `create-reply`) and a persistent mention-deduplication store.
- Thread context fetching and formatting for mention conversations.
- Cursor-based pagination on the post-fetching tools (auto-fetch, cursor and
  hours modes, capped totals).
- Self-hosted PDS support (`BLUESKY_SERVICE_URL`, `BSKY_WEB_URL`, and search
  through a separate unauthenticated agent against `api.bsky.app`).
- Removal of the upstream remote/OAuth HTTP mode (`src/remote/`, its
  Dockerfile, deploy artifacts, signing-key script and test); this server is
  stdio-only.
